1
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:13,380
Brighten up the peace,
then step back and see.

2
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:27,020
Hello, goodbye.

3
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:31,500
The one who heads home the
moment their errand is done.

4
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:35,280
Wahara, uwa, wahara.

5
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:39,980
Wawarabū watchi wawara.

6
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:45,560
Don't rush, in this narrow town.

7
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:49,380
What's this
"the safe way is the long way round"?

8
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:58,540
If perhaps there's someone better than me,

9
00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:02,960
tell me, tell me all through the night.

10
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:12,800
I don't mind waiting.

11
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:17,000
Because I'm a Kame-za woman.

12
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:21,740
I won't lose, Ginza woman.

13
00:01:21,740 --> 00:01:26,520
I'll love you for years and years.

14
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:30,020
The rainbow colors of the Kame-za woman.

15
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:39,660
A gift that blooms in the night sky.

16
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:49,260
It's 37 degrees in here!

17
00:01:49,260 --> 00:01:52,440
Don't check it, you'll only make it hotter!

18
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:55,460
I'm back, and I bought ice cream!

19
00:01:55,460 --> 00:01:56,420
Yay!

20
00:01:57,240 --> 00:02:00,260
Let's see,
and I also went and bought fireworks.

21
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:02,040
Reiko-san too?

22
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:04,780
I see.

23
00:02:05,560 --> 00:02:09,480
Besides, the senpai bought them straight
from a fireworks factory he knows.

24
00:02:09,480 --> 00:02:11,960
There are so many,
and it only cost 5,000 yen!

25
00:02:12,420 --> 00:02:16,080
Sure, it's cheap,
but what are we going to do with all this?

26
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:18,300
Isn't it obvious, Terai-kun?

27
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:21,220
We're holding a huge fireworks
show in the park out back!

28
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:26,700
So pretty.

29
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:29,380
Senko fireworks have such charm, don't they?

30
00:02:29,380 --> 00:02:32,020
I've got the same kind,
the ones that change color.

31
00:02:35,140 --> 00:02:36,740
We used to do this one a lot, didn't we?

32
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,240
That's right.

33
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:44,180
No, it's chasing after us!

34
00:02:44,180 --> 00:02:45,160
It came this way!

35
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:46,980
If you run, it follows you.

36
00:02:46,980 --> 00:02:48,340
Try staying still.

37
00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:52,820
This is Ryo-chan's doing again.

38
00:02:52,820 --> 00:02:54,080
What is this?

39
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:55,700
What is it, Nakagawa?

40
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:57,760
Don't you know about mouse fireworks?

41
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:00,960
I lived abroad when I was a kid, so

42
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:03,420
you can't predict how they move at all,
can you?

43
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:05,980
We used to play with them
all the time when we were kids.

44
00:03:05,980 --> 00:03:09,620
And when it comes to fireworks,
this is the one, no doubt about it.

45
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:11,060
Ta-da!

46
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:13,620
The king of fireworks, the aerial shell!

47
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:16,060
What a size!

48
00:03:16,060 --> 00:03:17,300
No way, Ryo-san!

49
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:18,920
Yeah, not here of all places!

50
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:21,260
What are you two talking about?

51
00:03:21,260 --> 00:03:23,540
Boom! A big blossom opens in the sky.

52
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:25,360
That's the real pleasure of fireworks,
isn't it?

53
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:30,140
This is a 200-shot salvo I made specially,
you know!

54
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:31,740
Get back!

55
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:44,020
It won't go up, you know.

56
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:46,240
That's strange.

57
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:51,920
Ohara, there doesn't seem to be anyone here.

58
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:55,340
That can't be right. Something's off.

59
00:03:57,180 --> 00:03:58,560
This time it'll be fine.

60
00:03:58,560 --> 00:03:59,880
Yo!

61
00:04:01,740 --> 00:04:03,340
Chief! The station head too!

62
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:08,200
What are you two doing in a place like this?

63
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:09,420
Well, you see...

64
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,980
You're hiding something behind your back.

65
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:13,200
No, nothing at all.

66
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:14,080
Don't lie to me!

67
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:16,240
No, really, it's the truth.

68
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:18,220
Just show me!

69
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:19,660
There's nothing at all!

70
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:33,000
There, there, there, there.

71
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:36,500
For real!

72
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:38,060
S-stay back!

73
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:42,800
Water! Water!

74
00:04:44,980 --> 00:04:46,020
Saved!

75
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:49,421
Ryotsu-kun,

76
00:04:49,471 --> 00:04:52,400
I trust you're prepared for this?

77
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:53,900
S-Shō-chan!

78
00:04:57,660 --> 00:04:59,960
This time, I absolutely won't forgive you.

79
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:01,500
Ryotsu is fired.

80
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:03,820
Your anger is completely justified, Chief.

81
00:05:03,820 --> 00:05:07,120
But firing him seems like too harsh a punishment,
don't you think?

82
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:09,720
He didn't mean any harm by it, you know.

83
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:12,760
If he meant harm,
firing him wouldn't be enough.

84
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:16,000
Besides, Ohara, you share the blame too.

85
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:19,900
This is what happens when
you've spoiled him all this time.

86
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:22,600
Hey, shall we go shopping on our day off?

87
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:23,160
Sounds good.

88
00:05:25,780 --> 00:05:27,240
Please, I'm begging you,
do something for us.

89
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:33,980
A pay cut?

90
00:05:35,220 --> 00:05:35,580
That's right.

91
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:38,880
Your salary this month will be cut by half.

92
00:05:39,820 --> 00:05:42,260
Fifty percent is half, isn't it?

93
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:43,680
No way.

94
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:47,020
I barely make anything as it is,
and if you cut it in half,

95
00:05:47,020 --> 00:05:48,380
I won't be able to survive.

96
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:50,020
Not my problem.

97
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:51,180
You brought it on yourself.

98
00:05:51,180 --> 00:05:53,740
Is it all right for your adorable
subordinate to starve to death?

99
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:56,760
You're not adorable. You're just a nuisance.

100
00:05:56,820 --> 00:05:59,780
If I die, I'll haunt you every day, Chief.

101
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:03,680
You can survive by eating
the weeds around here.

102
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:05,260
You demon, Chief!

103
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:09,080
Call me a demon or whatever you like.

104
00:06:09,130 --> 00:06:12,280
I'm tired of looking after you, too.

105
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:14,027
Saying all sorts of things,

106
00:06:14,077 --> 00:06:17,420
you really think I'll get in the way of your promotion,
don't you?

107
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:20,238
That's just how it is.
You can act like a nice guy all you want,

108
00:06:20,288 --> 00:06:24,100
but deep down you don't care
about your subordinates one bit.

109
00:06:24,900 --> 00:06:25,520
What did you say!

110
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:26,880
Ryo-chan, that's going too far!

111
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:28,320
That's right, senpai.

112
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:32,480
Hmph, you rich kids could never understand.

113
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:36,000
I'm not a rich kid, though.

114
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:38,680
You keep quiet!
You're making this more confusing!

115
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:39,600
W-well, maybe.

116
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:43,160
I won't think of you as a chief anymore,
you know.

117
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:46,740
Fine. I don't think of
you as a subordinate either!

118
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:47,620
Hmph!

119
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:48,140
Mm.

120
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:49,560
Mm.

121
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:50,060
Mm.

122
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:55,780
Yes, yes, this is Kōen-mae Police Box.

123
00:06:55,780 --> 00:06:57,340
Yes, yes.

124
00:06:58,140 --> 00:06:59,240
Chief.

125
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:01,180
It's from me.

126
00:07:01,180 --> 00:07:02,920
It's me.

127
00:07:03,700 --> 00:07:05,640
So it's been born!

128
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:06,920
Ha ha

129
00:07:06,920 --> 00:07:08,160
And how's Hiromi?

130
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:11,520
Please tell her she did well!

131
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:13,660
Chief, that just now...

132
00:07:13,660 --> 00:07:15,920
Your grandchild was born, then?

133
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:19,240
Wow, congratulations!

134
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:21,360
So that makes one boy and one girl, then.

135
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:24,820
My daughter asked me to come
up with a name for the baby.

136
00:07:24,820 --> 00:07:26,860
I've been thinking about it a lot, but

137
00:07:27,820 --> 00:07:29,540
how about Sakura?

138
00:07:29,540 --> 00:07:31,360
That's a lovely name, isn't it?

139
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:32,240
Really.

140
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:33,360
Y-you think so?

141
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:36,480
Isn't that a bit odd?

142
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:38,140
The eldest is Daisuke, right?

143
00:07:38,140 --> 00:07:40,740
If the eldest is Daisuke,
the younger one has to be Hanako.

144
00:07:40,740 --> 00:07:42,780
Then they'd be a comedy duo!

145
00:07:42,780 --> 00:07:45,740
Or else you'd name the eldest Torajirō,
or something.

146
00:07:47,620 --> 00:07:50,880
We might as well change our
surnames to Hayashi or Pei and Park.

147
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:51,860
Ryo-chan.

148
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:55,640
Now, now, there's no need to bother
with an idiot like this every time.

149
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:59,020
Anyway, once Hiromi is out of the hospital,
I'll prepare a feast.

150
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:01,260
Everyone, come and see my grandchild's face.

151
00:08:01,260 --> 00:08:02,620
A feast?

152
00:08:03,220 --> 00:08:06,360
It has nothing to do with you.
You're not my subordinate, after all.

153
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:10,140
I know, I know.
Newborn babies are all the same anyway.

154
00:08:10,140 --> 00:08:14,200
They all have the same monkey-like faces.
They're not the least bit interesting.

155
00:08:16,380 --> 00:08:18,380
How about the Sunday after next?

156
00:08:18,380 --> 00:08:20,680
There's a fireworks festival
at the riverbank nearby.

157
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,820
You can see it well from my garden.

158
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:24,200
That sounds great.

159
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,880
We'd be delighted to come over.

160
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:28,140
We should think of something
to give for the celebration.

161
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:31,000
No need to worry.

162
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:33,180
Even if you begged me, I wouldn't say it.

163
00:08:33,800 --> 00:08:36,040
But having my pay cut in half is rough.

164
00:08:36,040 --> 00:08:37,520
I've got to do something about it.

165
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:46,980
A part-time job? Ryo-san?

166
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:51,980
Right, this time of year there are fireworks festivals everywhere.
It's the busy season.

167
00:08:51,980 --> 00:08:54,320
Let me work too, will you?

168
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:57,480
Your pay's been cut
and you're in a real bind

169
00:08:58,320 --> 00:09:00,600
Well, it's busy, I'll admit.

170
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:03,020
After all, it's dangerous work.

171
00:09:03,020 --> 00:09:04,960
Even so,
suddenly being told it's a part-time job...

172
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:06,880
I've got plenty of experience, you know.

173
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:09,280
You've made fireworks before?

174
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:12,500
No fireworks, but when it comes
to explosions, I'm a veteran.

175
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,180
That'd be a problem, you know.

176
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:18,160
Because explosions and fireworks
are pretty much the same, right?

177
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:20,980
Sure, they both use gunpowder,
but they're totally different.

178
00:09:20,980 --> 00:09:23,560
Actually, aerial fireworks are

179
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:26,020
an art form in the sky,
created by craftsmen.

180
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:29,360
This is a star from a handmade firework.

181
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:31,360
While this star burns out,

182
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:33,860
it changes into three colors: red,
yellow, and blue.

183
00:09:33,860 --> 00:09:36,160
It's like a kawaridama.

184
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:39,860
As the many stars inside
the firework explode,

185
00:09:39,860 --> 00:09:42,720
they fly off in all directions,
changing color as they go.

186
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:46,420
If they just fly up, they scatter
everywhere and the colors won't line up.

187
00:09:46,420 --> 00:09:49,380
Unless they're launched in a circle,
they won't look beautiful.

188
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:54,020
That's why they're arranged like this,
so they spread out neatly in a sphere.

189
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:57,200
Calculating which color
changes into which color,

190
00:09:57,200 --> 00:10:00,180
you make the stars and
pack them in one by one.

191
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:03,720
I see, so it really is a craftsman's skill.

192
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:07,700
Exactly, so it's not suited for
people with sloppy personalities.

193
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:11,400
I'm meticulous,
you can tell just by looking at this face.

194
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:14,340
I also have a license for
handling hazardous materials.

195
00:10:14,340 --> 00:10:16,640
And the reason I got hired

196
00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:18,700
is all thanks to the fireworks here,
you know.

197
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:20,520
That's a baseless accusation.

198
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:23,160
If you help people while you're still alive,

199
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:24,920
you're sure to get something
good in the afterlife.

200
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:27,060
Don't kill people so easily.

201
00:10:27,060 --> 00:10:29,800
I've trained as a monk,
so I can chant sutras too.

202
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:31,120
I told you to stop.

203
00:10:31,860 --> 00:10:32,980
Well, I guess it can't be helped.

204
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:34,780
Yay! You'll hire me?

205
00:10:48,980 --> 00:10:51,320
Ryo-san, you've really gotten good at this,
haven't you.

206
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:52,607
Right? That's right.

207
00:10:52,657 --> 00:10:56,360
I've come up with a new fireworks idea.

208
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:57,880
A new firework?

209
00:10:58,120 --> 00:11:02,080
I'll give you the idea as a thank-you.
It's bound to be a huge hit.

210
00:11:05,460 --> 00:11:06,100
Like this,

211
00:11:06,150 --> 00:11:09,720
until now, fireworks had to
be lit one by one with candles.

212
00:11:10,280 --> 00:11:13,760
That was a hassle,
and the wind would blow the candle out.

213
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:18,180
I improved on that and combined it with a match.
This is it.

214
00:11:19,740 --> 00:11:22,640
Light it,
and it becomes a sparkler at the same time.

215
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:26,620
At ski resorts, you could have torch
girls use these for night skiing.

216
00:11:27,260 --> 00:11:28,240
This is going to be a hit.

217
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:36,200
That didn't work out so well earlier,
but this time it'll be fine.

218
00:11:37,640 --> 00:11:40,740
I call it the Great Serpent Fireworks!

219
00:11:41,620 --> 00:11:43,180
This one's spectacular!

220
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:48,640
This time it's definitely fine.

221
00:11:48,960 --> 00:11:50,160
They're message fireworks!

222
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:51,520
Message fireworks?

223
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:55,200
There's a light-emitting diode
mechanism built into the fireworks.

224
00:11:55,900 --> 00:11:58,440
You can freely program
messages into the LEDs,

225
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:01,300
and they unfold when it explodes.

226
00:12:01,780 --> 00:12:05,860
So the message appears in the night
sky the moment the fireworks open.

227
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:08,020
That's amazing!

228
00:12:08,020 --> 00:12:10,820
If that's true, it's bound to be a huge hit.

229
00:12:10,820 --> 00:12:11,360
Yeah.

230
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:14,700
By the way, this prototype has
"Banzai" programmed into it.

231
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:16,260
Let's launch it right away.

232
00:12:20,800 --> 00:12:22,780
Well, maybe I used too
much explosive powder.

233
00:12:22,780 --> 00:12:24,560
This is hopeless.

234
00:12:28,060 --> 00:12:31,500
Thanks for the meal.

235
00:12:33,260 --> 00:12:35,740
Ohara-san,
is that a photo of your grandchild?

236
00:12:36,220 --> 00:12:36,840
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

237
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:40,120
What a cute kid. How old is she?

238
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:43,680
She's three this year.
Her birthday's coming up soon.

239
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:46,500
I'm trying to figure out
what to get her as a present.

240
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:49,800
Are grandkids really that cute?

241
00:12:50,560 --> 00:12:52,020
Of course they are.

242
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:55,140
Just looking at this photo gives me energy.

243
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:58,860
I don't even have a wife,
let alone grandchildren.

244
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:01,840
Actually, right after this child was born,

245
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:04,480
the company I started myself went bankrupt.

246
00:13:05,740 --> 00:13:07,320
I was feeling really down,

247
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:09,880
but when I saw my
newborn grandchild's smile,

248
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:12,340
I felt like I had to do my best.

249
00:13:12,940 --> 00:13:13,880
So that's how I ended up here.

250
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:17,920
Yeah, I've known the president
here since we were kids.

251
00:13:18,620 --> 00:13:21,900
Honestly,
my grandchild is my source of energy.

252
00:13:24,780 --> 00:13:26,600
How about Sakura?

253
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:31,080
Now that I think about it,
the Chief also looked really happy.

254
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:33,989
That demon...

255
00:13:34,039 --> 00:13:38,260
It's the Chief's fault that I
have to work a part-time job here.

256
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:40,840
What's so great about a grandchild anyway?

257
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:59,080
Hey, have you decided on
a present for Sakura yet?

258
00:13:59,580 --> 00:14:01,240
That's the hard part.

259
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:04,920
I think something related to
the name Sakura would be nice.

260
00:14:06,060 --> 00:14:08,640
Hey, Ryo-chan, what are you planning to do?

261
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:10,220
Hey, I'm talking to you, Ryo-chan.

262
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:13,223
You're so annoying.
I'm exhausted from my part-time job.

263
00:14:13,273 --> 00:14:14,720
I don't care what the Chief thinks.

264
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:15,440
Well...

265
00:14:19,380 --> 00:14:21,360
Ryotsu has a part-time job?

266
00:14:22,080 --> 00:14:23,460
Yeah, apparently so.

267
00:14:23,460 --> 00:14:24,512
That idiot...

268
00:14:24,562 --> 00:14:28,500
Doesn't he have any intention
of getting by on his reduced pay?

269
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:31,800
Listen, don't tell anyone about this.

270
00:14:31,800 --> 00:14:33,758
If it reaches the president's ears,

271
00:14:33,808 --> 00:14:36,320
this time, no matter how much I beg him,

272
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:40,520
No, never mind. Anyway, I'm counting on you.

273
00:14:40,520 --> 00:14:41,180
Yes.

274
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:48,920
But you never get tired of
watching them all the time, do you?

275
00:14:48,920 --> 00:14:49,460
Yeah.

276
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:53,640
Speaking of which,
when the chief's first grandchild was born,

277
00:14:53,640 --> 00:14:56,020
he kept pulling out photos nonstop,

278
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:57,420
didn't he? He went on and on.

279
00:14:57,420 --> 00:14:59,440
The chief, of all people

280
00:15:00,020 --> 00:15:02,340
Calling him "chief" is far too good for him.

281
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:05,440
A boss who won't protect
his subordinates like that...

282
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:07,200
Just calling him by his name is plenty.

283
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:08,160
Do you think so?

284
00:15:08,160 --> 00:15:10,040
I don't think that's true.

285
00:15:12,940 --> 00:15:14,320
I told you before, didn't I?

286
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:17,880
I ran my own company too, small as it was.

287
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:24,240
Managing people means a lot of hardship behind
the scenes that those being managed never see.

288
00:15:25,300 --> 00:15:30,500
No matter how tight cash flow gets,
you have to think about their lives first.

289
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:30,800
You know?

290
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:37,400
Especially for middle management, you're
caught between those above and those below.

291
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:43,040
I'm sure you have plenty of worries. Our chief,
of all people, vents his stress with one word.

292
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:44,760
(continued from above)

293
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:47,120
I don't think that's true, though.

294
00:15:50,940 --> 00:15:53,660
Is this the place where
Ryotsu's doing his part-time job?

295
00:15:54,400 --> 00:15:55,500
Of all places.

296
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:57,900
The fireworks factory that angered the boss?

297
00:16:04,660 --> 00:16:05,540
Excuse me.

298
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:07,560
About that man just now...

299
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:08,840
How is he doing?

300
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:10,880
Is he working diligently?

301
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:13,520
You mean Ryo?

302
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:17,580
No, I'm not a suspicious person at all.

303
00:16:18,340 --> 00:16:20,360
Could you be the chief, by any chance?

304
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:21,600
Well that...

305
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:23,720
Ryo is always talking about you.

306
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:26,120
You really do worry about your subordinates,
don't you.

307
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:28,400
Sorry, my apologies, pardon me.

308
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:30,980
What's wrong?

309
00:16:30,980 --> 00:16:34,700
I was just thinking how nice the wind feels,
you know.

310
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:36,240
The wind, you see...

311
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:38,700
The wind.

312
00:16:42,460 --> 00:16:43,340
Reiko-san

313
00:16:44,280 --> 00:16:46,120
It's Komachi-chan and Naoko-chan.

314
00:16:46,560 --> 00:16:48,660
What are you doing in a place like this?

315
00:16:48,660 --> 00:16:50,540
I'm choosing a present.

316
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:53,800
A birthday present for
the chief's grandchild.

317
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:56,320
You mean Chief Ohara's?

318
00:16:56,460 --> 00:16:59,440
Yes, his second grandchild
was born recently.

319
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:02,720
We're all going to visit
tomorrow to see the baby.

320
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:03,380
I see.

321
00:17:04,240 --> 00:17:06,980
Speaking of Chief Ohara, the other day...

322
00:17:08,700 --> 00:17:14,340
What happened?
I saw something the other day... Actually,

323
00:17:16,800 --> 00:17:21,880
Please, I beg you, do something. I'll
take the same punishment as Ryotsu, so...

324
00:17:22,740 --> 00:17:31,800
Please overlook it just this once. The Chief said that,
and so both of them will have their salaries cut by half.

325
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:37,000
You really think they'll get in the way of his own promotion,
don't you?

326
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:40,280
He doesn't care about
his subordinates one bit.

327
00:17:42,180 --> 00:17:43,500
Ryo-chan, you have to tell him.

328
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:44,420
Reiko-san.

329
00:17:46,780 --> 00:17:48,180
Komachi,
what are you going to do about that?

330
00:17:48,780 --> 00:17:51,000
We won't have any luck with that for a while,
will we?

331
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,500
Before that, I want a boyfriend.

332
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:56,160
What, the Chief did that?

333
00:17:57,180 --> 00:17:59,440
Yes, Komachi-chan and the
others apparently saw it.

334
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:01,318
So what about it, Ryo-chan?

335
00:18:01,368 --> 00:18:04,840
Even after this, you're still going to
say the Chief only thinks about himself?

336
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:08,816
Come to Sakura-chan's
birthday party tomorrow,

337
00:18:08,866 --> 00:18:11,480
and apologize to the Chief! Understand?

338
00:18:12,460 --> 00:18:13,500
That's right, Ryo-san.

339
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:15,451
Even just now,

340
00:18:15,501 --> 00:18:18,980
he came secretly to check on you,
worried about you.

341
00:18:19,960 --> 00:18:20,840
The Chief did?

342
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:22,798
Perfect timing, then.

343
00:18:22,848 --> 00:18:25,500
The grandchild will step
in and help you make up.

344
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:29,400
That's right, Ryo-chan.
Come, okay? You have to!

345
00:18:30,220 --> 00:18:30,940
Yeah.

346
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:34,960
So, did Senpai say he'd come?

347
00:18:35,460 --> 00:18:37,242
Well, he hasn't really said for sure.

348
00:18:37,292 --> 00:18:39,780
I did press him to definitely come, though.

349
00:18:40,940 --> 00:18:43,080
Ryo-san can be stubborn, after all.

350
00:18:50,220 --> 00:18:52,280
This won't do! Damn it!

351
00:18:56,540 --> 00:18:58,257
Jō-san,

352
00:18:58,307 --> 00:19:00,860
what brings you here on a Sunday?

353
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:03,640
Hello!

354
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:07,579
I'm glad you came. Well, come in,

355
00:19:07,629 --> 00:19:10,580
please. Come on, Terai, hurry up too.

356
00:19:10,780 --> 00:19:12,960
Sorry for going to the
trouble of coming all this way.

357
00:19:13,220 --> 00:19:13,940
Wow!

358
00:19:14,700 --> 00:19:17,360
Dashike-kun.
You can say hello now, can't you?

359
00:19:17,580 --> 00:19:17,940
Right!

360
00:19:19,260 --> 00:19:21,700
Sakura just fell asleep.

361
00:19:22,820 --> 00:19:24,160
She's so adorable.

362
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:27,140
She really looks just like Hiromi-san.

363
00:19:27,140 --> 00:19:30,400
Yes, but her father
says she takes after him.

364
00:19:31,680 --> 00:19:34,320
She does, with those big bright eyes,
don't you think?

365
00:19:34,320 --> 00:19:36,640
Come to think of it, maybe so.

366
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:40,720
This is a baby outfit
as a congratulatory gift.

367
00:19:41,120 --> 00:19:45,580
Mine is an eco-friendly building block set for babies from zero years old,
for playing and learning.

368
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:48,360
Mine is an assortment of disposable diapers.

369
00:19:48,360 --> 00:19:50,940
Sorry, you really didn't
have to go to the trouble.

370
00:19:53,340 --> 00:19:54,540
Thank you, thank you.

371
00:19:55,160 --> 00:19:57,400
Dinner will be ready soon.

372
00:19:57,400 --> 00:19:59,940
Don't hold back. Make yourselves at home.

373
00:19:59,940 --> 00:20:00,640
Yes.

374
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:03,020
I wonder if Ryo-san isn't coming after all?

375
00:20:03,620 --> 00:20:04,740
Looks like it.

376
00:20:05,380 --> 00:20:06,760
After all I said to him?

377
00:20:07,660 --> 00:20:08,260
Done!

378
00:20:09,400 --> 00:20:10,540
Thanks, Miyasaka-san.

379
00:20:10,540 --> 00:20:11,880
It's all thanks to you.

380
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:14,300
Even though she's the Chief's granddaughter,

381
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:16,780
Hearing that, I can't just stay quiet.

382
00:20:16,780 --> 00:20:18,960
Give my regards to your grandchild too.

383
00:20:19,660 --> 00:20:20,840
Thank you for the meal.

384
00:20:20,840 --> 00:20:21,460
Thanks.

385
00:20:21,460 --> 00:20:22,680
I'm stuffed.

386
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:24,520
It feels like I ate Ryo-san's share too.

387
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:27,220
The fireworks show is about to start.

388
00:20:27,220 --> 00:20:29,460
You can see it really well from this garden.

389
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:33,500
There it goes!

390
00:20:33,500 --> 00:20:34,320
Beautiful.

391
00:20:34,320 --> 00:20:36,060
We really do have a great view.

392
00:20:36,420 --> 00:20:37,420
It's a front-row seat.

393
00:20:41,860 --> 00:20:43,680
I wonder what's happened to Ryo-chan.

394
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:45,020
Ryo-tsu?

395
00:20:46,780 --> 00:20:48,520
Forget about that guy.

396
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:50,940
Let's just relax and enjoy the fireworks.

397
00:20:58,220 --> 00:20:58,840
Sorry about this.

398
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:00,500
Thanks for giving me a ride.

399
00:21:00,500 --> 00:21:01,820
No explanations necessary!

400
00:21:01,820 --> 00:21:01,980
Ryo-san.

401
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,200
Ryo-san, it's already started!

402
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:08,980
Oh no, hurry!

403
00:21:08,980 --> 00:21:11,020
Easier said than done, but on this road...

404
00:21:11,020 --> 00:21:11,920
It'll work out somehow.

405
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:13,160
With enough spirit, anything is possible.

406
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:14,860
Whoa! That's cool! It's a shakudama!

407
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:17,120
Whoa! Fireworks!

408
00:21:17,300 --> 00:21:17,920
Ryo-san!

409
00:21:20,100 --> 00:21:23,980
Whoa! Oh no!
If it explodes here, we're done for!

410
00:21:28,760 --> 00:21:29,720
What the hell!

411
00:21:30,060 --> 00:21:32,780
Ow The fireworks!

412
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:34,960
Hey! Get back here!

413
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:44,300
Somebody catch that firework!

414
00:21:49,960 --> 00:21:51,620
It's still burning!

415
00:21:54,580 --> 00:21:55,240
Ryo-san!

416
00:22:00,280 --> 00:22:04,480
W-what happened?

417
00:22:12,420 --> 00:22:13,380
Ryotsu!

418
00:22:13,600 --> 00:22:14,500
Ryo-chan!

419
00:22:14,700 --> 00:22:16,500
Senpai! Ryo-san!

420
00:22:17,720 --> 00:22:23,780
Ryotsu, you idiot! What have you done this time,
you good-for-nothing?

421
00:22:24,320 --> 00:22:27,340
No, Chief, there's a deep reason for this.

422
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:32,940
This time, I'm truly fed up with you,
and I won't stand for it any longer!

423
00:22:32,940 --> 00:22:35,080
I told you there's a reason!

424
00:22:35,080 --> 00:22:37,860
I'm sure it's some stupid excuse,
knowing you.

425
00:22:41,340 --> 00:22:42,600
Dad, look!

426
00:22:42,600 --> 00:22:43,500
That firework!

427
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:45,500
This is...

428
00:22:59,180 --> 00:23:00,820
Yes! We did it, Ryo-san!

429
00:23:07,460 --> 00:23:09,360
A birthday celebration this amazing!

430
00:23:09,830 --> 00:23:11,840
Nobody but you would've
thought of this, senpai.

431
00:23:11,840 --> 00:23:13,720
Just like you, Ryo-chan.

432
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:15,960
Thanks, Ryo-san.

433
00:23:17,580 --> 00:23:18,280
Nyaa!

434
00:23:18,580 --> 00:23:19,480
Heh heh heh heh heh.

435
00:23:19,480 --> 00:23:21,540
It won't leave a physical trace,

436
00:23:21,590 --> 00:23:23,700
but it's a gift that stays in the heart

437
00:23:24,460 --> 00:23:25,100
Ryotsu.

438
00:23:25,900 --> 00:23:26,620
Chief.

439
00:23:35,280 --> 00:23:36,320
Y-yes!

440
00:23:36,660 --> 00:23:38,820
Hey, there's still some food left over,
isn't there?

441
00:23:39,040 --> 00:23:40,560
Yes! Still plenty!

442
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:42,420
Chief, is that really okay?

443
00:23:42,620 --> 00:23:45,920
Your household's had a tough month too,
hasn't it, Chief!

444
00:23:46,560 --> 00:23:48,260
It's all your fault, you idiot!

445
00:24:10,720 --> 00:24:14,700
In the gently passing seasons

446
00:24:15,860 --> 00:24:19,540
I've gotten good at making forced smiles.

447
00:24:20,760 --> 00:24:24,940
Swept along and changing, I wonder

448
00:24:25,820 --> 00:24:29,280
how I look in your eyes.

449
00:24:30,740 --> 00:24:36,140
After every fight,
we always share a brief kiss.

450
00:24:36,140 --> 00:24:40,240
I loved you with your teary eyes.

451
00:24:40,240 --> 00:24:45,480
Such irreplaceable things,

452
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:50,940
how many will a person
ever hold in a lifetime?

453
00:24:52,660 --> 00:24:57,260
You are me, and I am you,

454
00:24:58,080 --> 00:25:02,300
and that alone was enough to fulfill us.

455
00:25:03,240 --> 00:25:08,480
Just seeing you smile,

456
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:15,040
I felt every pain was healed.

457
00:25:22,100 --> 00:25:24,640
This is Ryotsu Physical Strength Co.

458
00:25:24,640 --> 00:25:27,000
From sports stand-ins to heavy labor,

459
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:29,260
if it involves using your body,
we're good to go.

460
00:25:29,260 --> 00:25:31,620
Write us a quick, reliable email.

461
00:25:31,620 --> 00:25:33,720
Ryotsu Physical Strength Co.

462
00:25:33,720 --> 00:25:36,740
Leave it to Ryotsu Physical Strength Co.

